  "reason": "The abstract discusses species differences in CYP3A induction and the role of the pregnane X receptor (PXR). While it mentions that compounds known to induce CYP3A in specific species also activate the corresponding PXR, and that PXR activation is predictive of CYP3A induction, it does not report a quantitative measure of agreement (e.g., concordance rate, PPV, sensitivity/specificity) between animal and human results. It focuses on the molecular mechanisms underlying species differences rather than quantifying the translational accuracy."
